## Collect ecommerce data

To collect ecommerce data, you need to add [ecommerce events](/analytics/answer/9267735#online-sales) to your website or app or in your Google Tag Manager container. Because these events require additional context to be meaningful, the events aren't sent automatically. Once you add the events and someone uses the website or app, you will start to notice ecommerce data in Analytics.&nbsp;

For more information about each event, read&nbsp;[Measure ecommerce](https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/collection/ga4/ecommerce?client_type=gtag).


 Note: If you manage your site using [Shopify](/analytics/answer/12183125) as your website builder or CMS, some events will be automatically tracked through the Shopify Pixel. 


