## Google Tag (Websites)



You can place ecommerce events anywhere below where you placed the Google tag. For example, all of the following spots are valid places for the events.



`&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;!-- Your tag goes here --&gt;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;!-- You can place ecommerce events here --&gt;
&nbsp; &nbsp; 
&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;title&gt;The title of the page&lt;/title&gt;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;!-- You can place ecommerce events here --&gt;`
`&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;!-- You can place ecommerce events here --&gt;`
`&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;!-- The part of your site that's shown to users --&gt;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &lt;!-- You can place ecommerce events here --&gt;`
`&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;`



 For more information about how to send events, read&nbsp;[Set up events](/analytics/answer/11147304). For information about placing your Google tag, read&nbsp;[About the Google tag](/analytics/answer/11994839).






